    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a high-efficiency trio led by **Vinnie Pasquantino** (75.15), **James Wood** (73.50), and **Corbin Carroll** (71.69). **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits significantly from the matchup against Bibee, where the 14% dynamic platoon advantage and 12% SP skill rating make him our top projected run-producer. Meanwhile, **James Wood** is locked into the leadoff spot against Tong, and his elite 0.404 xwOBA makes him the most dangerous asset in the lineup today. While **Corbin Carroll** and **Brice Turang** face a minor \"Elite Hold SP\" drag on their scores due to high-caliber defensive backstops capping their stolen base upside, the raw talent of **Corbin Carroll** in that #5 slot keeps his efficiency firmly in the \"Strong\" tier. **Isaac Paredes** (65.05) is also a sneaky play, buoyed by a substantial +10% park factor that makes him a primary source of power against Perkins.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Austin Riley** (54.30), who narrowly missed the cut behind the hot-hitting **Josh Naylor** (71.12). **Josh Naylor** holds a massive advantage today because of his matchup against Johnson; the +19% SP skill lift provided by the favorable matchup against Johnson is simply too high to leave on the pine. **Austin Riley** remains our primary depth piece, but his -3% park factor and the relative strength of the starting corner infielders kept him sidelined. We continue to monitor the status of **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Jose Caballero**, who remain inactive, while **Griffin Conine** fell well below our 40-point efficiency floor due to an unfavorable lefty-lefty matchup against Suter. With no major weather concerns across the board, the focus remains on leveraging the dynamic platoon advantages for **Mickey Moniak** and **Gabriel Moreno** to maximize our daily scoring output.",
